@startuml
title GC2D Domain Model and Simulation Lifecycle

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class Potential {
  Field model
}

class Dynamics {
  Equations of motion
}

class "Initial configuration\n(state geometry)" as InitialConfiguration {
  Initial physical state
  State layout and geometry
}

class "Initial-value problem" as InitialValueProblem {
  Dynamics + initial configuration
}

class "Numerical method" as NumericalMethod {
  Time-integration algorithm
}

class "Simulation request" as SimulationRequest {
  Time span, steps, output sampling
}

class "Simulation runner" as SimulationRunner {
  Validates and executes a run
}

class "Solution\n(computed trajectory)" as Solution {
  Immutable sampled times, states, diagnostics
}

Potential --> Dynamics : defines field forces
Dynamics --> InitialValueProblem
InitialConfiguration --> InitialValueProblem
InitialValueProblem --> SimulationRunner
NumericalMethod --> SimulationRunner
SimulationRequest --> SimulationRunner
SimulationRunner --> Solution : produces

note bottom of InitialConfiguration
  This role owns initial state geometry and
  component-major layout only. Physical rho
  and eta parameters belong to Dynamics.
end note

note bottom of Solution
  Solution is the read-only trajectory evolved in time.
  It is distinct from the initial-state
  geometry used to define a problem.
end note

note bottom of NumericalMethod
  Implicit ABBA 1 uses the reduced multiplier
  equation, while implicit ABBA 2 solves the
  equivalent simultaneous output-multiplier system.
  Both converge to the same projected physical map.
end note

note top of Potential
  Public APIs are grouped by responsibility in
  potential, dynamics, initial_conditions,
  simulation, diagnostics, studies, and visualization.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Concept |= Responsibility |
  | Potential | Physical field model |
  | Dynamics | Equations induced by the field model |
  | Initial configuration | Initial state and coordinate layout |
  | Simulation | Execution using a problem, numerical method, and request |
  | Solution | Computed trajectory and diagnostics |
endlegend

@enduml
